            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation><![CDATA[<summary>
            Attribute identifies the account for which to return transaction history.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <note type="caution"><!-- Failed to insert some or all of included XML --></note>
            </remarks>]]></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="DebitCreditOnly" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            D = Returns debit amounts only, C = Returns credit amounts only. Default is Null (all returned).
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="ExternalRtxnDescription" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Text to search in the External Transaction Description field. This criterion is logically OR-ed with IntRtxnDesc if it is not blank. 
            If this is left blank, field is not searched. White spaces and letter case will be ignored when looking for a match, e.g., the criterion ‗TRANSFERto' 
            will match 'Transfer To' in addition to other possibilities.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="FromAmount" nillable="true" type="xs:double">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Minimum amount for which history should be returned.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="FromCheckNumber" nillable="true" type="xs:long">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Start check number for which history should be returned.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="FromDate" nillable="true" type="xs:dateTime">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Start date for which history should be returned. 
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="InternalRtxnDescription" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Text to search in the Internal Transaction Description field. This criterion is logically OR-ed with ExtRtxnDesc if it is not blank. 
            If this is left blank, field is not searched. White spaces and letter case will be ignored when looking for a match, e.g., the criterion ‗TRANSFERto' 
            will match 'Transfer To' in addition to other possibilities.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="IsCustomerView" nillable="true" type="xs:boolean">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Providing the ability to display all transactions in the transaction history 
            irrespective of customer view indicator on the RTXNTYP is set to Y or N for employees/teller . Default is Y.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="IsErrorCorrect" nillable="true" type="xs:boolean">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Y = Returns error corrected transactions also, N = does not does not return EC transactions. Default is Y.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="IsIncludeBalanceDetail" nillable="true" type="xs:boolean">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Provide ability to display balance details of transaction if value provided is Y.Default is N.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="IsRejected" nillable="true" type="xs:boolean">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Y = Returns rejected transactions also, N = Returns only completed transactions. Default is Y.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="IsResultingBalance" nillable="true" type="xs:boolean">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Attribute value of Y requests that resulting balance (running balance) is returned. Possible values Y, N. 
            If a value of Y is specified, FromDate must be supplied and TransactionReferenceNbr must not be supplied. This flag is ignored if account is masterline. 
            Default is N. Even when value of N is supplied, running balance is returned if FromDate and ThruDate are the ONLY criteria supplied; and SortBy 
            is set to null or TIMEUNIQUEEXTN.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="IsReversed" nillable="true" type="xs:boolean">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Y = Returns reversed transactions also, N = does not does not return reversed transactions. Default is Y.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="MaximumRows" nillable="true" type="xs:long">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Attribute identifies the maximum number of rows to return.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="PreviousRunningBalance" nillable="true" type="xs:double">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The balance to use as a starting value. This value would be provided in a continuation request.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="RtxnReportGroupCodes" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            List of RTXN Report Group Codes to retrieve separated by commas.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="RtxnTypeCodes" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            List of RTXN Type Codes to retrieve separated by commas, e.g., SPMT, PRCT.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="SearchDateOption" nillable="true" type="xs:int">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>		
            Indicates the date to use to display balance details of transaction history in response. (1 = Activity Date, 2 = Post Date) Default is 2
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="SortBy" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Indicates which value to sort by. Options are: RTXNNBR, CHECKNBR, TIMEUNIQUEEXTN, RTXNTYPCD, POSTDATE, EFFDATE, TRANAMT, RTXNTYPDESC. 
            Default is TIMEUNIQUEEXTN
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="SortOrder" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            The sort order. A = Ascending, D = Descending. Default is Ascending.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="ThroughAmount" nillable="true" type="xs:double">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Maximum amount for which history should be returned.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="ThroughCheckNumber" nillable="true" type="xs:long">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            End check number for which history should be returned.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="ThroughDate" nillable="true" type="xs:dateTime">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            End date for which history should be returned.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="TimeUniqueExtension" nillable="true" type="xs:long">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            Attribute identifies the time unique extension from which to start the query.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element minOccurs="0" name="TransactionReferenceNumber" nillable="true" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:appinfo/>
              <xs:documentation>&lt;summary>
            AcctNbr-RtxnNbr The only other search criteria this tag can be combined with is the acctNbr attribute; the others will be ignored.
            &lt;/summary></xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
        </xs:sequence>
      </xs:extension>
    </xs:complexContent>
  </xs:complexType>
